/* AI brain Q&A pack 08: PC help & this Windows 12 sim */
(window.AIQA = window.AIQA || []).push(
  ["is this real windows | is this the real windows 12 | is windows 12 real | is this a real computer", "Nope! This is a pretend Windows 12 computer that runs inside your web browser, made just for fun. It isn't made by or connected to Microsoft, and nothing here can change your real computer."],
  ["is this made by microsoft | are you affiliated with microsoft | did microsoft make this", "No — this Windows 12 sim is a fan-made project and is not affiliated with or endorsed by Microsoft. The app names and looks are just for pretend play."],
  ["is the money real | is my bank balance real money | can i spend real money here", "All money in this sim is pretend. Your **Forge Bank** balance, Store purchases, Game Pass and Copilot plans use fake money, so nothing ever charges a real card."],
  ["should i type my real password | can i use my real password here | is it safe to enter my real email password", "Please don't! Never type a real password, real credit card number or other private info into this pretend computer. Make up a simple PIN or password just for the sim."],
  ["are the accounts real | is my microsoft account here real | is the sign in real", "No, the accounts in this sim are pretend. Signing in here doesn't log you into any real Microsoft, Google or other account."],
  ["what is this website | what is this app | what am i looking at", "You're using a pretend Windows 12 computer in your browser. It has a desktop, taskbar, Start menu, Settings, File Explorer, a Microsoft Store, Edge, Office apps, games like Mincraft and The Sims, and me — Copilot!"],
  ["where is my stuff saved | where does this save my files | does this save my progress", "Everything you do here is saved in this web browser on this device. If you clear your browser data or use a different browser or device, the sim starts fresh."],
  ["will my files be here next time | does it remember me | will my apps still be here tomorrow", "Yes — as long as you use the same browser on the same device and don't clear its site data, your apps, files, wallpaper and settings will be waiting for you."],
  ["can this harm my computer | can this give me a virus | is this sim safe", "This sim is just a web page, so it can't install anything on your real computer or change your real files. Its 'viruses', 'installers' and 'updates' are all pretend."],
  ["who are you | what are you | what can you do copilot", "I'm Copilot, the built-in helper in this Windows 12 sim. I can explain how to use the apps and settings here, share PC tips and shortcuts, and answer lots of everyday questions."],
  ["are you connected to the internet | are you a real ai | do you use chatgpt", "I'm an offline helper — I answer by matching your question to a big list of answers I already know. I don't browse the internet, so if I don't know something, try rewording your question."],
  ["what is copilot | what does copilot do | what is the copilot app", "Copilot is your AI helper in this sim. Click the **Copilot** button on the taskbar (or the desktop icon) and type a question in **Message Copilot**, then press **Enter**."],
  ["how do i open copilot | where is copilot | how to start copilot", "Click the colorful **Copilot** button near the right side of the taskbar, or double-click the **Copilot** icon on the desktop."],
  ["how do i start a new chat | new copilot chat | how to start over with copilot", "In Copilot, click **New chat** at the top of the left sidebar. Your older chats stay listed under **Recent**."],
  ["how do i delete a chat | remove a copilot conversation | delete chat history", "In the Copilot sidebar under **Recent**, hover a chat and click the little **X** next to it. To empty just the chat you're in, click **Clear** at the top."],
  ["what is copilot plus | what is copilot+ | what do i get with copilot+", "**Copilot+** is the middle plan: 150 messages a day, up to 3 attachments per message and 3 image creations a day, for $4.99 a month of pretend money."],
  ["what are the copilot plans | copilot plan prices | copilot subscription options", "There are three plans:\n1. **Basic** — free, 15 messages a day, 1 attachment, no images.\n2. **Copilot+** — $4.99/mo, 150 messages, 3 attachments, 3 images a day.\n3. **Advanced** — $9.99/mo, unlimited messages and attachments, 5 images a day.\nAll prices are pretend money."],
  ["how many messages can i send | what is the message limit | how many questions can i ask a day", "On the free **Basic** plan you get 15 messages a day. **Copilot+** gives 150 a day and **Advanced** is unlimited. The count resets each new day, and you can see what's left next to the send button."],
  ["i ran out of messages | copilot says i used all my messages | message limit reached", "You've hit today's limit for your plan. Wait until tomorrow for it to reset, or click **Upgrade Copilot** in the sidebar to pick a bigger plan (paid with pretend Forge Bank money)."],
  ["how do i upgrade copilot | how to get copilot plus | buy copilot advanced", "In Copilot, click **Upgrade Copilot** at the bottom of the sidebar, then choose **Get Copilot+** or **Get Advanced**. It's billed to your pretend Forge Bank balance."],
  ["what is copilot advanced | advanced plan copilot | what does the advanced plan include", "**Advanced** is the top Copilot plan: unlimited messages, unlimited attachments and 5 image creations a day for $9.99 a month (pretend money)."],
  ["can copilot make pictures | how do i make an image with copilot | generate an image copilot", "Yes, on **Copilot+** or **Advanced**. Click **Create** in the Copilot sidebar or type something like 'Create an image of a dragon'. The free Basic plan can't make images. You can also try the **Image Studio** app."],
  ["how do i attach a file to copilot | send a picture to copilot | upload file copilot", "Click the paperclip **Attach file** button in the message box and pick a file. Basic allows 1 attachment per message, Copilot+ allows 3, and Advanced is unlimited."],
  ["can copilot talk | how do i use voice with copilot | make copilot read out loud", "Click the microphone **Voice mode** button to speak your question, and use the speaker toggle at the top to have replies read aloud (your browser has to support it)."],
  ["how do i downgrade copilot | switch back to basic | cancel copilot plan", "Open **Upgrade Copilot** in the Copilot sidebar and click **Switch to Basic**."],
  ["how do i lock my computer | how to lock the pc | lock my screen", "Open **Start**, click the power button at the bottom-right, then choose **Lock**. On a real Windows PC you can also press **Windows + L**."],
  ["how do i unlock it | how to sign in on the lock screen | unlock the pc", "Type your PIN or password in the box on the lock screen and press **Enter** (or click the arrow). If you set up a fingerprint, you can click **Touch ID** instead."],
  ["i forgot my pin | forgot my password | i cant remember my pin", "No problem! On the lock screen, click **Forgot PIN?** and type a new one. A PIN must be 4 or 6 digits. You'll be signed right in."],
  [["how do i change my password | how to change my pin | change sign in pin", "Lock the PC (**Start** → power → **Lock**), then click **Forgot PIN?** on the lock screen and enter your new PIN or password. A PIN has to be 4 or 6 digits."], "Open **Settings** → **Accounts** → **Sign-in options**, type your new PIN (4 to 6 numbers) or password twice and click **Change**. If you're locked out, click **Forgot PIN?** on the lock screen."],
  ["what does skip test mode do | skip button on lock screen | what is test mode", "**Skip (test mode)** on the lock screen lets you into the desktop without typing your PIN. It's there for testing — it's handy, but it means anyone using this browser can get in."],
  ["my pin doesnt work | it says incorrect try again | wrong pin on lock screen", "Check that Caps Lock is off and you're typing the same PIN you made during setup. If you still can't remember it, click **Forgot PIN?** to set a new one."],
  ["how do i put the computer to sleep | sleep mode | how to sleep the pc", "Open **Start**, click the power button and choose **Sleep**. The screen goes dark — click it to wake up, and you'll see the lock screen."],
  ["how do i restart | how to restart the computer | reboot the pc", "Open **Start**, click the power button at the bottom-right and choose **Restart**. The sim reloads and your stuff is still saved."],
  ["how do i shut down | how to turn off the computer | power off", "Open **Start**, click the power button and choose **Shut down**. The screen fades out and then starts back up, since this is a pretend PC — to really stop, just close the browser tab."],
  ["where is the power button | power options | how do i find lock sleep restart", "Click **Start**, then the power symbol at the bottom-right corner of the Start menu. You'll see **Lock**, **Sleep**, **Restart** and **Shut down**."],
  ["what is the difference between sleep and shut down | sleep vs shutdown | should i sleep or shut down", "**Sleep** pauses the computer so it wakes up fast, right where you left off. **Shut down** turns it fully off. On a real PC, sleep is great for short breaks, and a full shut down or restart now and then keeps things running smoothly."],
  ["what is a pin | why use a pin instead of a password | what is windows hello", "A PIN is a short number code (here 4 or 6 digits) you use to sign in. Windows Hello is the name for quick sign-in options like PIN, face or fingerprint."],
  ["can i use a password instead of a pin | use letters in my pin | password with letters", "Yes. During setup on the **Set up a PIN** screen, tick the option to include letters and symbols, and it becomes a password instead."],
  ["how do i set up fingerprint | touch id sign in | use fingerprint to unlock", "Fingerprint sign-in is offered during setup on the **Fingerprint** screen. If you set it up, a **Touch ID** button shows on the lock screen."],
  [["how do i factory reset | reset this pc | start over from scratch", "Open **Settings** → **System** → **Factory Reset**. You'll type your PIN twice, then type CONFIRM. You can choose to keep your icons, apps and wallpaper, or wipe everything. You can also type factory-reset in **Terminal**."], "Open **Settings** → **System** → **Recovery** and click **Reset PC**. You'll type your PIN twice, then type CONFIRM. You can choose to keep your icons, apps and wallpaper, or wipe everything. You can also type factory-reset in **Terminal**."],
  ["what happens if i factory reset | will reset delete my stuff | does factory reset erase everything", "Factory Reset takes you back through setup. It asks whether to keep your icons, installed apps and wallpaper (OK) or wipe everything (Cancel), so read that box carefully."],
  [["how do i run setup again | redo the windows setup | go through setup again", "Use **Settings** → **System** → **Factory Reset**. After confirming, the sim restarts and walks you through setup again."], "Use **Settings** → **System** → **Recovery** → **Reset PC**. After confirming, the sim restarts and walks you through setup again."],
  [["what is a product key | do i need a product key | how do i activate windows", "A product key is a 25-character code (XXXXX-XXXXX-XXXXX-XXXXX-XXXXX) that activates Windows. In this sim it's asked for during setup; you can choose **I don't have product key** to use a trial. **Settings** → **Account** shows if you're activated."], "A product key is a 25-character code (XXXXX-XXXXX-XXXXX-XXXXX-XXXXX) that activates Windows. In this sim it's asked for during setup; you can choose **I don't have product key** to use a trial. **Settings** → **System** → **Activation** shows if you're activated."],
  [["is my windows activated | check activation | activation status", "Open **Settings** → **Account**. It shows **Windows activation: Activated** with your key, or **Not activated**."], "Open **Settings** → **System** → **Activation**. It shows **Active** with your product key, or **Not active**."],
  [["how do i change my username | change my account name | rename my user", "Your name is chosen during setup. To pick a new one, run setup again with **Settings** → **System** → **Factory Reset**."], "Open **Settings** → **Accounts** → **Your info**, type a new name under **Your name** and click **Save**. Your new name shows in Settings, on the lock screen and in Start."],
  [["how do i change my profile picture | change account picture | change my avatar", "Your account picture is picked during setup. You can see it in **Settings** → **Account**, on the lock screen and at the bottom of **Start**. Doing a Factory Reset lets you choose again."], "Open **Settings** → **Accounts** → **Your info** and click **Browse files** to choose a photo. Click **Remove** to go back to the default picture."],
  [["where do i see my account | account info | who am i signed in as", "Click your name at the bottom-left of **Start**, or open **Settings** → **Account**. It shows your username, email (if any), sign-in type and activation."], "Click your name at the top of **Settings** (or open **Settings** → **Accounts**). It shows your name, your email (or **Local Account**) and that you're an Administrator."],
  ["what is the start menu | where is the start button | how do i open start", "Click the Windows logo on the taskbar to open **Start**. It has a search box, your **Pinned** apps, **Recommended** recent apps, your name, and the power button."],
  ["how do i find an app | where are all my apps | find a program", "Open **Start** and type the app's name in the search box, or click **Search Anything** on the taskbar. All your installed apps are listed under **Pinned** in Start."],
  ["what does recommended in start show | recent apps in start menu | what is recommended", "**Recommended** in Start shows the apps you opened most recently, so you can jump back in quickly."],
  ["how do i make a group in start | start menu folders | group apps in start", "Start menu groups like **Office** and **Essentials** hold several apps. Right-click a group to **Rename group** or **Delete group**."],
  ["how do i use search | what is search anything | search bar on taskbar", "Click **Search Anything** on the taskbar and start typing. You'll see matching apps, a quick answer card for famous names, dictionary definitions for single words, and a **See web results** link."],
  ["can search define words | dictionary in search | look up a word meaning", "Yes! Type a single word into **Search Anything** on the taskbar and a **Dictionary** card shows its meaning."],
  ["what is the taskbar | what is the bar at the bottom | taskbar explained", "The taskbar is the bar at the bottom of the screen. From left to right: **Widgets** (weather), **Search Anything**, **Start**, pinned apps (Store, Edge, File Explorer, Photos), open windows, **Copilot**, quick settings and the clock."],
  ["how do i change the taskbar style | taskbar layout | make the taskbar classic", "Right-click an empty part of the taskbar and pick a **Taskbar layout**: **Default**, **Joined**, **Classic** or **Compact**."],
  ["what happens when i right click a taskbar icon | jump list | close all windows of an app", "Right-clicking an app on the taskbar shows its jump list with **Open**, any quick actions, and **Close all windows** if it's running."],
  ["what are widgets | how do i open widgets | weather on the taskbar", "Click the weather and temperature at the far left of the taskbar to open **Widgets**. You'll see weather, a clock, a **To do** list and a stock **Watchlist**."],
  ["how do i add a to do in widgets | widget task list | add a task to widgets", "Open **Widgets** from the left of the taskbar, type in **Add a task**, then click **Add** or press **Enter**. Tick the box when it's done or click × to remove it."],
  ["is the weather real | where does the weather come from | weather is wrong", "If you allow location and you're in the US, Widgets and the **Weather** app can show real forecasts from the US weather service. Otherwise they show sample weather."],
  ["how do i see notifications | notification center | where did my notification go", "Click the clock on the right of the taskbar to open **Notifications**, along with a calendar. Click **Clear all** to empty the list."],
  ["how do i stop notifications | turn off pop ups | mute notifications", "Turn on **Focus** in quick settings (click the Wi-Fi/volume/battery icons on the taskbar). Pop-ups stop showing, but they're still saved in the notification center."],
  ["what are quick settings | where is the wifi button | volume and brightness controls", "Click the Wi-Fi, volume and battery icons near the bottom-right of the taskbar. Quick settings has tiles for **Wi-Fi**, **Bluetooth**, **Airplane mode**, **Focus**, **Night light** and **Cast**, plus brightness and volume sliders."],
  ["how do i change the volume | turn the sound up | mute the sound", "Open quick settings by clicking the volume or Wi-Fi icon on the taskbar and drag the volume slider. Slide it all the way left to mute."],
  ["how do i change the brightness | make the screen darker | screen too bright", "Open quick settings from the taskbar (Wi-Fi/volume/battery icons) and drag the sun slider left to dim the screen or right to brighten it."],
  ["what is night light | how do i turn on night light | make the screen warmer", "**Night light** gives the screen a warm, orange tint that's easier on your eyes at night. Turn it on with the **Night light** tile in quick settings."],
  ["what is focus mode | focus tile | do not disturb", "**Focus** is like do-not-disturb: notification pop-ups stay hidden so you can concentrate. Toggle it with the **Focus** tile in quick settings."],
  ["how do i check my battery | battery percentage | is my laptop charging", "Click the quick settings icons on the taskbar; the battery percentage shows at the bottom. If your device shares battery info with the browser, it shows your real battery level."],
  ["how do i open settings | where is settings | open the settings app", "Double-click the **Settings** icon on the desktop, find **Settings** in **Start**, or right-click the desktop and choose **Personalize**."],
  [["what is in settings | settings sections | what can i change in settings", "Settings has **Personalization**, **Network & internet**, **Bluetooth & devices**, **Accessibility**, **Account**, **Time & language**, **Personalize icons**, **Windows Update** and **System**."], "Settings has **System**, **Bluetooth & devices**, **Network & internet**, **Personalization**, **Apps**, **Accounts**, **Time & language**, **Gaming**, **Accessibility**, **Privacy & security** and **Windows Update**. Use **Find a setting** at the top left to search all of them."],
  [["how do i change my wallpaper | change the background | change desktop picture", "Open **Settings** → **Personalization** and click one of the wallpapers under **Background**. You can also pick a **Solid color** or click **Upload an image** to use your own picture."], "Open **Settings** → **Personalization** → **Background** and click one of the pictures. You can also pick a **Solid color** or click **Browse photos** to use your own picture. Tip: right-click the desktop → **Personalize** jumps straight there."],
  [["how do i use my own picture as wallpaper | upload a wallpaper | set a photo as background", "Go to **Settings** → **Personalization** and click **Upload an image** at the bottom, then pick a picture from your device. It becomes your desktop and lock screen background."], "Go to **Settings** → **Personalization** → **Background** and click **Browse photos**, then pick a picture from your device. It becomes your desktop and lock screen background."],
  [["how do i make the background a plain color | solid color wallpaper | one color background", "Open **Settings** → **Personalization** and click any square under **Solid colors**."], "Open **Settings** → **Personalization** → **Background** and click any square under **Solid colors**."],
  ["how do i change the lock screen picture | lock screen wallpaper | change lock screen background", "The lock screen uses the same background as your desktop, so change it in **Settings** → **Personalization** → **Background**."],
  [["how do i switch to dark mode | turn on dark mode | make windows dark", "Open **Settings** → **Accessibility** and click **Dark** under **Appearance**. Click **Light** to switch back."], "Open **Settings** → **Accessibility** and turn on **Dark mode**. Turn it off to go back to light."],
  [["how do i switch to light mode | turn off dark mode | make it bright again", "Open **Settings** → **Accessibility** and click **Light** under **Appearance**."], "Open **Settings** → **Accessibility** and turn off **Dark mode**."],
  [["how do i change my accent color | change the theme color | change highlight color", "Open **Settings** → **Personalization** and scroll to **Accent color**. Click one of the color circles, or use **Custom** to pick any color or type a hex code."], "Open **Settings** → **Personalization** and click **Colors**. Pick one of the Windows colors, or use **Custom color** to choose any color or type a hex code."],
  [["how do i get the windows xp theme | make it look like windows xp | xp mode", "Open **Settings** → **Personalization**, scroll to **Theme**, and click **Windows XP**. It switches to the classic green-hills Bliss wallpaper and a retro look. Click **Windows 12** to go back."], "Open **Settings** → **Personalization**, click **Themes**, and choose **Windows XP**. It switches to the classic green-hills Bliss wallpaper and a retro look. Choose **Windows 12** to go back."],
  [["how do i make text bigger | increase font size | text is too small", "Open **Settings** → **Accessibility** and drag the **Text size** slider. It goes from 80% up to 180%."], "Open **Settings** → **Accessibility** and drag the **Text size** slider. It goes from 80% up to 180%. (It's also in **System** → **Display**.)"],
  [["how do i turn on the on screen keyboard | virtual keyboard | type without a keyboard", "Open **Settings** → **Accessibility** and click **Toggle on-screen keyboard**. Click a text box, then tap the keys on screen. Click the button again to hide it."], "Open **Settings** → **Accessibility** and turn on **On-screen keyboard**. Click a text box, then tap the keys on screen. Turn it off to hide it."],
  [["what accessibility options are there | accessibility settings | help for people who need it easier", "**Settings** → **Accessibility** lets you switch Light/Dark appearance, change **Text size**, and turn on the **on-screen keyboard**. Quick settings also has **Night light** and brightness."], "**Settings** → **Accessibility** has **Text size**, **Dark mode** and the **On-screen keyboard**. **Settings** → **Personalization** can also turn off animations, transparency and shadows, and **System** → **Display** has brightness and **Night light**."],
  ["how do i turn off wifi | turn on wi-fi | wifi settings", "Click the Wi-Fi icon on the taskbar and tap the **Wi-Fi** tile, or open **Settings** → **Network & internet** and flip the **Wi-Fi** switch."],
  ["what is airplane mode | how do i turn on airplane mode | turn off airplane mode", "**Airplane mode** turns off wireless radios like Wi-Fi and Bluetooth. Toggle it in quick settings or in **Settings** → **Network & internet**. Turning Wi-Fi back on switches airplane mode off."],
  ["why does my wifi say weak signal | wifi signal strength | change wifi to strong", "In **Settings** → **Network & internet**, the **Signal strength** buttons let you pick **Strong** or **Weak** for the pretend Wi-Fi. The taskbar icon changes to match."],
  ["what wifi am i connected to | network name | which network is this", "The sim pretends you're connected to **HomeNetwork_5G**. You can see it in **Settings** → **Network & internet**. (Your real browser uses your real connection either way.)"],
  ["how do i turn on bluetooth | bluetooth settings | connect bluetooth", "Open quick settings from the taskbar and tap the **Bluetooth** tile. In this sim it's a pretend switch, so it won't pair real devices."],
  ["how do i change mouse settings | mouse speed | pointer speed", "Open **Settings** → **Bluetooth & devices**. Under **Mouse** you can change **Pointer speed**, **Scrolling speed** and which button is primary."],
  ["how do i swap mouse buttons | left handed mouse | change primary mouse button", "Go to **Settings** → **Bluetooth & devices** → **Mouse** and set **Primary mouse button** to **Right** (or back to **Left**)."],
  [["how do i change the time format | 24 hour clock | switch to 12 hour time", "Open **Settings** → **Time & language** and click **Toggle 12/24-hour**."], "Open **Settings** → **Time & language** → **Date & time** and turn **24-hour clock** on or off."],
  [["how do i change the language | change region | time and language settings", "**Settings** → **Time & language** shows your region, language and clock style. Region and language are picked during setup; you can redo them with a Factory Reset."], "Open **Settings** → **Time & language**. **Windows display language** changes the language, and **Language & region** shows your region and format."],
  ["how do i update windows | windows update | check for updates", "Open **Settings** → **Windows Update** and click **Download & install all**. When it finishes, click **Restart now**. If you're already up to date, click **Check for updates**."],
  ["do i need to restart after an update | update says restart required | restart now after update", "Yes — after **Windows Update** installs, click **Restart now** so the updates finish. In this sim the updates are pretend, but it's a good real-life habit."],
  [["how do i change app icons | custom icons | personalize icons", "Open **Settings** → **Personalize icons**, find the app, and click **Upload** to pick an image. You can also right-click a desktop icon and choose **Change icon…**."], "Open **Settings** → **Personalization** → **Personalize icons**, find the app, and click **Upload** to pick an image. You can also right-click a desktop icon and choose **Change icon…**."],
  [["what does the system page in settings do | settings system | system info", "**Settings** → **System** shows that this is the Windows 12 simulation build and has the red **Factory Reset** button."], "**Settings** → **System** shows your name and has **Display**, **Sound**, **Notifications**, **Power & battery**, **Storage**, **Activation**, **Recovery** (reset this PC) and **About** (rename your PC and see its specs)."],
  ["how do i close a window | close an app | how to exit a program", "Click the **X** (Close) button in the top-right corner of the window. You can also right-click its taskbar button and choose **Close all windows**."],
  ["how do i minimize a window | hide a window | make a window go away without closing", "Click the **–** (Minimize) button at the top-right of the window. Click the app's taskbar button to bring it back."],
  ["how do i maximize a window | make a window full screen | make the window bigger", "Click the square **Maximize** button at the top-right of the window. Click it again (**Restore down**) to go back to the smaller size."],
  ["how do i move a window | drag a window | move app around the screen", "Click and hold the window's title bar (the top strip with its name), then drag it where you want. On a touch screen, drag the title bar with your finger."],
  ["how do i snap windows side by side | split screen | snap layouts", "This sim doesn't have snap layouts. Drag windows by their title bars to arrange them, or click **Maximize** to fill the screen. On a real Windows PC, press **Windows + Left/Right arrow** to snap."],
  ["how do i switch between windows | go to another app | switch apps", "Click the app's button on the taskbar, or click any visible part of the window you want. On a real PC, **Alt + Tab** flips between open windows."],
  ["my window disappeared | where did my app go | i cant find my open window", "It's probably minimized. Look for its button on the taskbar and click it. If it's not there, it was closed — just open the app again."],
  ["an app is frozen in the sim | app not responding | how do i end a task", "Open **Task Manager** (Microsoft Store → **Task Manager** → **Open**), go to **Processes**, and click **End task** next to the app. Or just close its window with the **X**."],
  ["what is task manager | how do i open task manager | see running apps", "**Task Manager** shows your running apps and background processes, and live CPU, memory, disk and network graphs. Open it from the Microsoft Store (Utilities → **Task Manager** → **Open**). On a real PC, press **Ctrl + Shift + Esc**."],
  ["what is the run box | how do i open run | win r", "The **Run** dialog opens an app by typing its name, like notepad, calc, mspaint, cmd, explorer or control. Press **Windows + R** (if your keyboard sends it), or open **Run** from the Microsoft Store."],
  ["how do i add an icon to the desktop | put an app on the desktop | desktop shortcut", "Apps you get from the **Microsoft Store** show up on the desktop automatically. To add another copy of an icon, right-click it and choose **Duplicate**."],
  ["how do i delete a desktop icon | remove an icon | get rid of an app icon", "Right-click the icon and choose **Delete**. It goes to the **Recycle Bin**, where you can **Restore** it later. Deleting a Store app's icon also uninstalls it."],
  ["how do i uninstall an app | remove an app i installed | delete a program", "Right-click the app's desktop icon and choose **Delete**. Store apps get uninstalled and moved to the **Recycle Bin**. To get it back, open the Recycle Bin and click **Restore**, or get it again from the Store."],
  ["what is the recycle bin | where do deleted things go | open recycle bin", "The **Recycle Bin** is the first icon on the desktop. Deleted icons go there so you can **Restore** them. Click **Empty Recycle Bin** to clear it for good."],
  ["how do i restore something i deleted | undelete | get back a deleted icon", "Double-click **Recycle Bin** on the desktop and click **Restore** next to the item."],
  ["how do i empty the recycle bin | clear the trash | permanently delete", "Open the **Recycle Bin** from the desktop and click **Empty Recycle Bin**. Items emptied from there can't be restored."],
  ["how do i make icons bigger or smaller | change desktop icon size | small icons", "Right-click an empty spot on the desktop, point to **View**, and pick **Large icons**, **Medium icons** or **Small icons**."],
  ["how do i sort desktop icons | arrange icons | organize my desktop", "Right-click an empty area of the desktop, point to **Sort by**, and choose **Name** or **Type**."],
  ["what is an app group | how do i make a folder on the desktop | group desktop icons", "An **App Group** is like a folder for desktop icons. Select some icons, right-click one and choose **App Group**, then type a name. Click the group to open it."],
  ["how do i select multiple icons | select many icons at once | drag to select", "Click and drag on an empty part of the desktop to draw a box around the icons you want. Then right-click one of them to act on all of them."],
  ["how do i rename an app group | rename a group | change group name", "Right-click the group and choose **Rename**, then type the new name."],
  ["how do i copy and paste an icon | cut and paste on desktop | duplicate a shortcut", "Right-click an icon and choose **Copy** (or **Cut**), then right-click an empty spot on the desktop and choose **Paste**."],
  ["what does refresh do on the desktop | refresh desktop | desktop not updating", "Right-click the desktop and choose **Refresh** to redraw your icons. It's handy if something looks out of place."],
  ["what is on the right click menu | desktop right click options | context menu", "Right-clicking the desktop shows **View**, **Sort by**, **New**, **Add to app group**, **Paste**, **Refresh**, **Personalize** and **Display settings**."],
  ["how do i open an app on the desktop | double click doesnt work | open desktop icon", "Double-click the icon with a mouse. On a touch screen, tap it once to select it, then tap again (or right-click/long-press and choose **Open**)."],
  ["how do i open file explorer | where are my files | open my documents", "Click the folder icon on the taskbar to open **File Explorer**. On the left you'll see **OneDrive**, **Desktop**, **Documents**, **Downloads**, **Pictures**, **Videos** and **Music**."],
  ["how do i make a new folder | create a folder | new folder in file explorer", "In **File Explorer**, go to where you want it and click **New folder** in the toolbar. Then use the **⋮** menu on it to **Rename** it."],
  ["how do i rename a file | rename a folder | change a file name", "In **File Explorer**, click the **⋮** (More) button on the file or folder, choose **Rename**, type the new name, and click **OK**."],
  ["how do i delete a file | delete a folder in file explorer | remove a file", "In **File Explorer**, click the **⋮** button on the item, choose **Delete**, and confirm."],
  ["how do i make a text file | new text document | create a txt file", "In **File Explorer**, click **New text file**. It opens right away so you can type. Or open **Notepad** for quick notes."],
  ["how do i make a word document | new docx | create a document", "In **File Explorer**, click **New Word document**, or open **Word** from the desktop and start typing."],
  ["how do i go back a folder | go up a folder | navigate in file explorer", "In **File Explorer**, click the **↑** (Up) button, or click a name in the path bar (like **This PC**) to jump back."],
  ["can i open real files from my computer | open a file from my device | view my own photos", "Yes — apps like **Media Player**, **VLC** and **Adobe Acrobat**, plus the **Upload an image** wallpaper button, can open files from your real device using your browser's file picker. The file is only viewed; nothing on your device is changed."],
  ["what is onedrive | onedrive folder | cloud storage", "OneDrive is Microsoft's cloud storage for keeping files online. In this sim, **OneDrive** is a folder in File Explorer, but files only live in this browser."],
  ["how do i take a screenshot | snipping tool | screen capture", "Open **Snipping Tool** (Microsoft Store → **Snipping Tool** → **Open**), click **New**, then drag a box over the part of the screen you want. Click **Save to Photos** or **Copy**. On a real PC, press **Windows + Shift + S**."],
  ["where do my screenshots go | where are snips saved | find my snip", "Click **Save to Photos** in Snipping Tool and the snip is kept in **Photos**. Recent snips also show at the bottom of Snipping Tool."],
  ["how do i cancel a snip | stop snipping | escape snipping tool", "Press **Esc** while the snip overlay is showing, or just click without dragging."],
  ["what is the photos app | how do i see my pictures | open photos", "Click the **Photos** icon on the taskbar to see your pictures, including snips you saved from Snipping Tool."],
  ["how do i use notepad | open notepad | write a quick note", "Open **Notepad** from **Start** and just start typing. It's a simple plain-text editor — no fancy formatting."],
  ["how do i use paint | draw a picture | open paint", "Open **Paint** (get it from the Microsoft Store if it isn't in Start). Pick a color, use the slider to set brush size, and drag on the canvas to draw. Click **Clear** to start over."],
  ["how do i use the calculator | open calculator | do math on the computer", "Double-click **Calculator** on the desktop. Click the number buttons and +, −, ×, ÷, then **=**. **C** clears, **±** flips the sign and **%** divides by 100."],
  ["how do i use the clock | timer | stopwatch", "Open the **Clock** app from Start. It has a countdown timer, world clock and stopwatch."],
  ["how do i use sticky notes | to do app | make a reminder list", "Get **Sticky Notes** or **To Do** from the Microsoft Store for quick notes and checklists. The **Widgets** panel also has a little **To do** list."],
  ["how do i use the terminal | command prompt | what commands can i type", "Get **Terminal** from the Microsoft Store, open it and type help. You can try dir, cd, mkdir, calc (2+3)*4, color green, ping, ipconfig, open settings, and even wsl --install arch."],
  ["how do i install linux | wsl arch | arch linux in terminal", "In **Terminal**, type wsl --install arch and wait for it to finish, then type arch to enter. Type exit to go back. It's a fun simulation — no real Linux is installed."],
  ["what is windows security | is my pc protected | virus scan", "**Windows Security** (Windows Defender) shows virus & threat protection, firewall and device health. Open it from the Microsoft Store. In this sim it's pretend, but on a real PC keep it turned on!"],
  ["what is the tips app | tips for windows 12 | how do i learn more features", "Open **Tips** from the Microsoft Store for quick ideas, like searching anything, personalizing your PC, asking Copilot and getting more apps."],
  ["what are achievements | how do i see my achievements | achievements app", "The **Achievements** app tracks milestones you reach across Windows 12 apps. Open it from **Start**."],
  ["how do i use the color picker | find a hex code | pick a color", "Open **Color Picker** from the Microsoft Store. Drag in the big square and the rainbow bar to choose a color, then click **Copy** to copy its HEX code. It also shows RGB and HSL."],
  ["how do i make a qr code | qr code generator | turn a link into a qr code", "Open the **QR Code** app from Start, type any text or link, and it makes a scannable QR code."],
  ["how do i install apps | how to download an app | how do i get new apps", "Open the **Microsoft Store** (the bag icon on the taskbar), find an app, and click **Get**. It installs right away and appears on your desktop and in Start."],
  ["what is the microsoft store | where is the store | open the store", "The **Microsoft Store** is where you get new apps and games. Click the Store icon on the taskbar or desktop. Use the categories on the left like **Games**, **Productivity**, **Utilities** and **Multimedia**."],
  ["why does the store say open instead of get | app already installed | store button says open", "**Open** means you already have that app installed — click it to launch the app. **Get** means it's not installed yet."],
  ["are store apps free | do apps cost money | how much do apps cost", "Most Store apps are free — just click **Get**. Anything that costs money uses your pretend **Forge Bank** balance, never real money."],
  ["some store apps dont do anything | store app just shows a picture | app is only a placeholder", "A few Store listings are just for show and open a simple placeholder window. Most others are real working apps and games."],
  ["what games are there | what games can i play | list of games", "There's lots! In the Store: **Mincraft**, **The Sims**, **Stardew Valley**, **DOOM**, **Solitaire**, **Snake**, **Pong**, **2048**, **Minesweeper**, **Breakout**, **Tic-Tac-Toe**, **Memory Match** and more. The **Xbox** app has even more, like Microsoft Flight Simulator and GTA VI."],
  ["how do i get minecraft | how do i play minecraft | where is minecraft", "Double-click the **Minecraft** icon on the desktop to open the **Minecraft Launcher**, then press **Play**. You already own it, so it's ready to go!"],
  ["how do i play mincraft | what is mincraft | mincraft controls", "**Mincraft** is the block-building sandbox: mine, build and explore. Use **W A S D** (or arrows) to move, the mouse to look, **Space** to jump, left-click to mine, right-click to place, **1–9** to pick a hotbar slot, **E** for inventory and **Esc** for the menu."],
  ["how do i open my inventory in minecraft | minecraft inventory key | crafting in mincraft", "Press **E** to open your inventory and crafting. Press **E** or **Esc** to close it."],
  ["how do i get minecraft mods | curseforge | install mods", "Open **CurseForge** from Start to browse and install pretend Minecraft mods."],
  ["how do i play the sims | how do i get the sims | where is the sims", "Open the **Microsoft Store**, go to **Games**, and click **Get** on **The Sims**. Then open it to create a Sim, look after their needs, get a job and furnish their house. It's also in the **Xbox** app."],
  ["how do i take care of my sim | sims needs | my sim is unhappy", "Watch your Sim's needs: **Hunger**, **Comfort**, **Hygiene**, **Bladder**, **Energy**, **Fun**, **Social** and **Room**. Click objects like the fridge, shower, bed or TV to pick actions that fill up the low bars."],
  ["how do i get a job in the sims | sims career | make money in the sims", "In The Sims, pick a career for your Sim. They catch the carpool to work and earn money, and building skills helps them get promoted."],
  ["how do i buy furniture in the sims | sims buy mode | decorate my sims house", "Switch to **Buy mode** in The Sims to shop for furniture and objects, then place them around your house."],
  ["how do i get stardew valley | play stardew | farming game", "Click **Get** on **Stardew Valley** in the Microsoft Store (under Games). You inherit your grandpa's farm — grow crops, forage, fish and ship your harvest."],
  ["how do i play doom | get doom | shooter game", "Click **Get** on **DOOM** in the Microsoft Store's Games section. It's a retro tribute to the 1993 classic with two maps. It's rated for older players, so check with a grown-up first."],
  ["how do i play solitaire | card game | klondike", "Open **Microsoft Solitaire** from the Store (it's already installed, so it says **Open**). It's classic Klondike: build the four piles from Ace to King by suit."],
  ["what is the xbox app | how do i use xbox | xbox game pass", "The **Xbox** app is a game store with **Game Pass**. Buy games or join **Game Pass Ultimate** ($16.99/mo of pretend money) to play lots of included titles. Click **Play** on a game you own."],
  ["how do i join game pass | cancel game pass | get xbox game pass", "In the **Xbox** app, click **Join** on the Game Pass banner to subscribe with pretend Forge Bank money. Click **Cancel Game Pass** in the same spot to stop it."],
  ["how do i play gta | grand theft auto vi | get gta 6", "**Grand Theft Auto VI** is in the **Xbox** app — buy it with pretend money, then click **Play**. Walk up to a car and press **E** to drive. It's rated M (17+), so it's for older players only."],
  ["how do i play flight simulator | microsoft flight simulator | fly a plane", "Find **Microsoft Flight Simulator** in the **Xbox** app, get it (or use Game Pass), and click **Play**. Press **H** to toggle the cockpit heads-up display."],
  ["what do the game ratings mean | esrb rating | is this game ok for kids", "Games in the Xbox app show an ESRB rating: **EC** early childhood, **E** everyone, **E10+** ages 10 and up, **T** teen, **M** mature 17+. The Common Sense Media button shows a suggested age."],
  ["i dont have enough money | insufficient funds | not enough balance", "Your pretend **Forge Bank** balance is too low for that. Check it by opening the **Bank** bookmark in Edge. Remember, it's all play money!"],
  ["what is forge bank | where is my money | check my balance", "**Forge Bank** is the sim's pretend bank. Open **Edge** and click the **Bank** bookmark to see your balance and transactions. Store, Xbox and Copilot purchases come out of it."],
  ["can i get a refund | refund an app | undo a purchase", "Some purchases, like paid Store apps, are marked refundable in your **Forge Bank** transactions. Open the Bank site in Edge to check. It's all pretend money anyway."],
  ["how do i open the internet | how do i browse the web | open edge", "Click the **Edge** icon on the taskbar or desktop. Type a search or website in the address bar and press **Enter**. **Chrome** is on the desktop too."],
  ["what are the bookmarks in edge | favorites bar | built in websites", "The bookmarks bar in Edge has the sim's built-in sites: **Bank**, **Amazon**, **Microsoft**, **YouTube**, **Discord**, **Duolingo**, **Netflix**, **FlightStats** and **DoorDash**. They're pretend versions."],
  ["how do i go back in edge | back button browser | reload a page", "Use the **←** (Back), **→** (Forward) and **↻** (Reload) buttons at the top-left of Edge. The house button takes you home."],
  ["how do i save a website | add to favorites in edge | bookmark a page", "In Edge, click the **Add to favorites** button next to the address bar."],
  ["can edge read pages out loud | read aloud | listen to a web page", "Yes — click the **Read aloud** speaker button next to Edge's address bar."],
  ["why wont a website load | page is blank | site refused to connect", "Many real websites block being shown inside other pages, so they may not load in this pretend browser. Try the built-in bookmark sites, or open the real site in a new tab of your actual browser."],
  ["how do i watch youtube | open youtube | youtube app", "Double-click the **YouTube** icon on the desktop, or click the **YouTube** bookmark in Edge. It's a pretend YouTube with famous channel names."],
  ["how do i use word | write a document | microsoft word", "Double-click **Word** on the desktop. Type on the page and use the ribbon for bold, italic, fonts, sizes and colors. It saves as you type, and **Ctrl + S** saves too."],
  ["how do i use excel | make a spreadsheet | excel formulas", "Open **Excel** from the desktop. Click a cell and type numbers or text. Formulas start with =, like =SUM(A1:A3) to add up cells A1 to A3."],
  ["how do i use powerpoint | make a slideshow | make a presentation", "Open **PowerPoint** from the desktop to build slides, then present them as a slideshow."],
  ["how do i send an email | outlook | write an email", "Open **Outlook** from Start, click to compose a new message, fill in **To**, a subject and your message, then send. It's pretend email — nothing actually leaves the sim."],
  ["what is onenote | take notes in onenote | notebooks", "**OneNote** is a digital notebook with notebooks, sections and pages for organizing notes. Open it from Start."],
  ["how do i make a quiz | microsoft forms | make a survey", "Open **Forms** from the desktop to build a survey or quiz and collect responses."],
  ["what is canva | how do i make a poster | design a logo", "**Canva** is on your desktop. Use it to design posts, posters, logos and slides by dragging things around."],
  ["can word write for me | ai in word | generate text in word", "Yes — Word has an AI button that writes text from your description. You can also try the **AI Text** app."],
  ["what is microsoft 365 | buy office | office bundle", "**Microsoft 365** opens the Microsoft site in Edge where you can pick an Office bundle with pretend money. Word, Excel, PowerPoint, Outlook, OneNote and Forms are already in the sim to try."],
  ["how do i read a pdf | open a pdf file | adobe acrobat", "Open **Adobe Acrobat** from Start and open a PDF from your device to read it."],
  ["how do i play music or videos | media player | play an mp3", "Open **Media Player** or **VLC** and click to open a video or audio file from your device. It plays right inside the sim."],
  ["how do i use the camera | take a selfie | camera app", "Get **Camera** from the Microsoft Store. Your browser will ask permission to use your webcam — only allow it if you're okay with that."],
  ["how do i record my voice | voice recorder | record audio", "Get **Voice Recorder** from the Microsoft Store. Your browser will ask to use the microphone first."],
  ["how do i chat with messenger | messenger app | talk to people in messenger", "Open **Messenger** from the desktop to chat with pretend tech personas. They're characters, not real people, so never share private info."],
  ["how do i learn a language | duolingo | language lessons", "Open **Duolingo** from Start for fun, bite-sized language lessons."],
  ["how do i use translator | translate words | translation app", "Get **Translator** from the Microsoft Store and type text to translate it."],
  ["how do i check the weather | weather app | forecast", "Click the weather at the left of the taskbar for Widgets, or open the **Weather** app from the Microsoft Store for a full forecast."],
  ["how do i use maps | find a place | maps app", "Get **Maps** from the Microsoft Store to browse a map. It needs an internet connection to load."],
  ["how do i see a calendar | calendar app | what day is it", "Click the clock on the taskbar to see this month's calendar, or open the **Calendar** app from the Microsoft Store."],
  ["how do i code | vs code | code editor", "Open **Visual Studio Code** or **Code Editor** from Start to write HTML, CSS and JavaScript with a live preview. In VS Code, **Ctrl + Shift + P** opens the command palette."],
  ["how do i use google classroom | classroom app | my assignments", "Get **Google Classroom** from the Microsoft Store to see pretend classes, announcements and assignments."],
  ["how do i use gmail | gmail app | check my gmail", "Get **Gmail** from the Microsoft Store. It's a pretend inbox with tabs, a reading pane, stars and compose."],
  ["how do i make an ai image | image studio | text to image", "Open **Image Studio** from Start, describe the picture you want, and generate it. Copilot+ and Advanced plans can also make images in Copilot."],
  ["what is the cafe app | order food | sip and bite cafe", "Get **Sip & Bite Café** from the Store to order pretend drinks, snacks and meals and earn reward stars."],
  ["how do i use blender | 3d modeling | blockbench", "Get **Blender** or **Blockbench** from the Microsoft Store (Multimedia) to play with simple 3D models — switch shapes, recolor and rotate them."],
  ["how do i use powershell | windows powershell | run as administrator", "Open **Windows PowerShell** from the Microsoft Store (it's under Utilities and says **Open**) to try command-line cmdlets in a pretend console."],
  ["what keyboard shortcuts are there | useful keyboard shortcuts | list of shortcuts", "Handy ones:\n**Ctrl + C** copy, **Ctrl + X** cut, **Ctrl + V** paste, **Ctrl + Z** undo, **Ctrl + Y** redo, **Ctrl + A** select all, **Ctrl + S** save, **Ctrl + F** find, **Ctrl + P** print, **Alt + Tab** switch windows, **Windows + D** show desktop, **Windows + L** lock, **Windows + E** File Explorer, **Ctrl + Shift + Esc** Task Manager. (Some Windows-key shortcuts only work on a real PC.)"],
  ["how do i copy | what does ctrl c do | copy shortcut", "Select the text or item, then press **Ctrl + C** (on a Mac, **Cmd + C**). It's copied to the clipboard, ready to paste."],
  ["how do i paste | what does ctrl v do | paste shortcut", "Click where you want it and press **Ctrl + V** (on a Mac, **Cmd + V**) to paste what you last copied or cut."],
  ["how do i cut | what does ctrl x do | cut and paste", "Select something and press **Ctrl + X** to cut it (it's removed and kept on the clipboard), then press **Ctrl + V** where you want to move it."],
  ["how do i undo | what does ctrl z do | undo a mistake", "Press **Ctrl + Z** (Mac: **Cmd + Z**) to undo the last thing you did. Press it again to undo more steps."],
  ["how do i redo | what does ctrl y do | redo shortcut", "Press **Ctrl + Y** to redo something you undid. In many apps **Ctrl + Shift + Z** works too (Mac: **Cmd + Shift + Z**)."],
  ["how do i select all | what does ctrl a do | highlight everything", "Press **Ctrl + A** (Mac: **Cmd + A**) to select everything in the document, text box or folder."],
  ["how do i save | what does ctrl s do | save shortcut", "Press **Ctrl + S** (Mac: **Cmd + S**) to save your work. Save often so you don't lose anything! In this sim's Word, **Ctrl + S** works too."],
  ["how do i find a word on a page | what does ctrl f do | search a page", "Press **Ctrl + F** (Mac: **Cmd + F**), type the word, and the app highlights where it appears. Press **Enter** to jump to the next match."],
  ["how do i print | what does ctrl p do | print a page", "Press **Ctrl + P** (Mac: **Cmd + P**) to open the print window, choose your printer and settings, then click **Print**."],
  ["what does alt tab do | how do i switch apps with the keyboard | alt tab", "Hold **Alt** and tap **Tab** to flip between open windows on a real PC. Let go of Alt to switch to the highlighted one. (Your browser's real OS may catch this, so in the sim just click the taskbar.)"],
  ["what does windows d do | show the desktop | hide all windows", "On a real Windows PC, **Windows + D** hides all windows to show the desktop; press it again to bring them back. In the sim, minimize windows with their **–** buttons."],
  ["what does windows l do | lock shortcut | windows key l", "**Windows + L** instantly locks a real Windows PC. In this sim, use **Start** → power → **Lock**."],
  ["what does windows e do | open file explorer shortcut | windows key e", "On a real Windows PC, **Windows + E** opens File Explorer. In this sim, click the folder icon on the taskbar."],
  ["what does ctrl shift esc do | task manager shortcut | open task manager quickly", "On a real Windows PC, **Ctrl + Shift + Esc** opens Task Manager straight away so you can close a frozen app."],
  ["what does ctrl alt delete do | ctrl alt del | three finger salute", "On a real Windows PC, **Ctrl + Alt + Delete** opens a screen where you can lock, switch user, sign out, change your password or open Task Manager."],
  ["what does windows shift s do | screenshot shortcut | snip shortcut", "On a real Windows PC, **Windows + Shift + S** opens the snipping toolbar so you can capture part of the screen to the clipboard."],
  ["what does print screen do | prtsc key | prt sc", "The **Print Screen** (PrtSc) key copies a picture of the whole screen to the clipboard on most PCs. Paste it into Paint, Word or a chat with **Ctrl + V**."],
  ["what does windows v do | clipboard history | see things i copied", "On a real Windows PC, **Windows + V** shows your clipboard history so you can paste something you copied earlier. You may need to turn it on the first time."],
  ["what does windows period do | emoji keyboard | how do i type emoji", "On a real Windows PC, press **Windows + .** (period) to open the emoji picker. On a Mac, press **Ctrl + Cmd + Space**."],
  ["what does ctrl t do | open a new tab | new browser tab", "In most web browsers, **Ctrl + T** opens a new tab and **Ctrl + W** closes the current tab. **Ctrl + Shift + T** brings back a tab you closed by accident."],
  ["what does f5 do | refresh a web page | reload shortcut", "**F5** (or **Ctrl + R**) reloads the current web page. **Ctrl + F5** does a harder refresh that skips the cache."],
  ["what does alt f4 do | close window shortcut | alt f4", "On a real PC, **Alt + F4** closes the window you're using. If you're on the desktop, it opens the shut-down menu. Save your work first!"],
  ["how do i zoom in on a web page | make the page bigger | ctrl plus", "Press **Ctrl + +** to zoom in, **Ctrl + -** to zoom out, and **Ctrl + 0** to reset. You can also hold **Ctrl** and scroll the mouse wheel."],
  ["what does ctrl b do | make text bold | bold italic underline shortcuts", "In most text editors, **Ctrl + B** is bold, **Ctrl + I** is italic and **Ctrl + U** is underline."],
  ["how do i type a capital letter | shift key | caps lock", "Hold **Shift** while pressing a letter for one capital. Press **Caps Lock** to type ALL capitals, and press it again to turn it off."],
  ["what is the windows key | where is the windows key | start key", "The Windows key has the Windows logo and sits near the bottom-left of the keyboard between **Ctrl** and **Alt**. Pressing it opens Start on a real Windows PC."],
  ["what are function keys | f1 to f12 | what does f1 do", "The **F1–F12** keys along the top do special jobs that depend on the app: **F1** often opens help, **F2** renames a selected file, **F5** refreshes, and **F11** toggles full screen in browsers."],
  ["how do i make a folder on my computer | create a folder on windows | new folder shortcut", "On a real Windows PC, right-click an empty spot in a folder or on the desktop and choose **New** → **Folder**, or press **Ctrl + Shift + N** in File Explorer. Type a name and press **Enter**."],
  ["how do i rename a file on windows | f2 rename | rename on a real pc", "Click the file once to select it, press **F2** (or right-click → **Rename**), type the new name, and press **Enter**. Be careful not to change the extension after the dot."],
  ["what is a file extension | what does .txt mean | file type ending", "A file extension is the letters after the dot in a file name, like .txt, .jpg, .mp3 or .docx. It tells the computer what kind of file it is and which app should open it."],
  ["how do i see file extensions | show file extensions | hidden file types", "On a real Windows PC, open File Explorer, click **View** → **Show** → **File name extensions**. On a Mac, Finder → **Settings** → **Advanced** → **Show all filename extensions**."],
  ["what are common file types | jpg vs png | list of file extensions", "Common ones: **.jpg/.png** pictures, **.mp3** music, **.mp4** video, **.pdf** documents that look the same everywhere, **.docx** Word files, **.xlsx** Excel files, **.txt** plain text and **.zip** compressed folders."],
  ["how do i zip files | how to compress a folder | make a zip file", "On Windows, select the files, right-click and choose **Compress to ZIP file** (or **Send to** → **Compressed (zipped) folder**). On a Mac, right-click and choose **Compress**."],
  ["how do i unzip a file | extract a zip | open a zip folder", "On Windows, right-click the .zip file and choose **Extract All**, then pick where to put the files. On a Mac, just double-click the .zip."],
  ["what is a zip file | why zip files | what does compressed mean", "A zip file squishes one or more files into a single smaller package. It's great for sending lots of files at once or saving space."],
  ["how do i move a file | drag files into a folder | move files between folders", "Drag the file onto the folder you want, or select it, press **Ctrl + X** to cut, open the new folder and press **Ctrl + V** to paste."],
  ["how do i find a lost file | search my computer for a file | where did my file go", "On a real Windows PC, open File Explorer and type the name in the search box at the top right, or check the **Downloads** and **Recent** areas. On a Mac, use **Spotlight** (**Cmd + Space**)."],
  ["where do downloads go | find my downloads | downloads folder", "Most browsers save files to your **Downloads** folder. In a browser, press **Ctrl + J** (Mac: **Cmd + Shift + J** in Chrome) to see recent downloads."],
  ["what is the clipboard | where does copied stuff go | clipboard meaning", "The clipboard is a hidden spot that holds what you last copied or cut, so you can paste it somewhere else. Copying something new replaces it."],
  ["my computer is slow | why is my pc so slow | how to speed up my computer", "Try these:\n1. Close apps and browser tabs you aren't using.\n2. Restart the computer.\n3. Install updates.\n4. Delete files and apps you don't need to free space.\n5. Run a virus scan.\nIf it's still slow, ask a grown-up or tech helper."],
  ["my computer is frozen | screen is stuck | computer wont respond", "1. Wait a minute — it may be busy.\n2. Press **Ctrl + Shift + Esc** to open Task Manager and **End task** on the stuck app.\n3. If nothing works, hold the power button for about 10 seconds to force it off, wait, then turn it on. You may lose unsaved work."],
  ["an app wont close | program not responding | force quit an app", "On Windows, open Task Manager (**Ctrl + Shift + Esc**), select the app and click **End task**. On a Mac, press **Cmd + Option + Esc** and choose **Force Quit**."],
  ["why should i restart my computer | does restarting help | turn it off and on again", "Restarting clears out stuck programs and memory and finishes installing updates. 'Turn it off and on again' really does fix lots of problems!"],
  ["how do i restart a real windows pc | restart windows 11 | reboot windows", "Click **Start**, click the power icon, and choose **Restart**. Save your work first."],
  ["how do i update my real computer | update windows 11 | install windows updates", "On Windows, open **Settings** → **Windows Update** → **Check for updates**, then install and restart. On a Mac, go to **System Settings** → **General** → **Software Update**."],
  ["why are updates important | should i install updates | do i need updates", "Updates fix bugs and patch security holes that bad guys could use, and sometimes add new features. Installing them keeps your device safer and running better."],
  ["my computer has no sound | sound not working | cant hear anything", "1. Check the volume isn't muted (taskbar speaker icon).\n2. Make sure headphones or speakers are plugged in and turned on.\n3. Check the app or video's own volume.\n4. Pick the right output device in sound settings.\n5. Restart the computer."],
  ["my wifi isnt working | no internet connection | cant connect to the internet", "1. Make sure Wi-Fi is on and airplane mode is off.\n2. Turn Wi-Fi off and on again.\n3. Move closer to the router.\n4. Restart your computer.\n5. Ask a grown-up to restart the router (unplug for 30 seconds). Check if other devices work too."],
  ["my mouse isnt working | mouse wont move | cursor stuck", "Check the mouse is plugged in or its batteries are charged, try a different USB port, and clean the bottom sensor. For Bluetooth mice, turn Bluetooth off and on. A restart often helps too."],
  ["my keyboard isnt typing | keys not working | keyboard stopped working", "Make sure it's plugged in or charged, check that **Num Lock** or **Caps Lock** isn't confusing things, try another USB port, and restart. Make sure the text box you want is clicked first."],
  ["my screen is upside down | screen rotated | display sideways", "On Windows, open **Settings** → **System** → **Display** and set **Display orientation** to **Landscape**. On some PCs, **Ctrl + Alt + Up arrow** also fixes it."],
  ["my battery drains fast | save battery | make laptop battery last longer", "Lower the screen brightness, close apps you aren't using, turn on battery saver, turn off Bluetooth if you don't need it, and unplug accessories."],
  ["how do i clear my browser cache | clear cache | clear browsing data", "In Chrome or Edge, press **Ctrl + Shift + Delete**, pick a time range, tick **Cached images and files**, and click **Clear data**. Clearing cookies too will sign you out of websites."],
  ["what is cache | what are cookies | what is browser cache", "**Cache** is a stash of website pieces your browser keeps so pages load faster. **Cookies** are small notes websites save to remember things like your sign-in or settings."],
  ["what is incognito mode | private browsing | inprivate window", "Incognito (Chrome) or InPrivate (Edge) is a window that doesn't save your history or cookies after you close it. Open one with **Ctrl + Shift + N** in Chrome or Edge (Firefox: **Ctrl + Shift + P**). It does NOT make you invisible online."],
  ["how do i clear my history | delete browsing history | erase history", "In most browsers, press **Ctrl + H** to open History and choose **Clear browsing data**, or press **Ctrl + Shift + Delete** and tick **Browsing history**."],
  ["how do i make a strong password | good password tips | create a secure password", "Make it long (at least 12 characters), use a mix of words, numbers and symbols, and don't use your name or birthday. A silly passphrase like 'Purple-Taco-Rocket-42!' is strong and easy to remember."],
  ["should i use the same password everywhere | reuse passwords | one password for all sites", "No — use a different password for each important account. If one site gets hacked, the others stay safe. A password manager can remember them for you."],
  ["what is a password manager | how do i remember all my passwords | password manager", "A password manager is an app that safely stores all your passwords behind one main password. Many browsers have one built in. Ask a grown-up which one your family uses."],
  ["what is two factor authentication | what is 2fa | two step verification", "Two-factor authentication (2FA) means you need your password AND a second thing, like a code sent to your phone, to sign in. It makes accounts much harder to break into."],
  ["should i share my password | can i tell my friend my password | sharing passwords", "Keep your passwords private — only share them with a parent or trusted grown-up. Real companies will never ask for your password in a message or call."],
  ["how do i spot a scam | is this a scam | signs of a scam", "Watch out for messages that: rush you ('act now!'), offer prizes that sound too good to be true, ask for passwords, codes, gift cards or money, have odd spelling or strange links, or come from someone pretending to be a company or friend. When in doubt, don't click — ask a trusted adult."],
  ["what is phishing | phishing email | fake email asking for password", "Phishing is a trick where scammers send fake emails, texts or websites that look real to steal your passwords or money. Never enter your password from a link in a message — go to the site yourself."],
  ["a website says i have a virus | pop up says call microsoft | tech support scam", "That's a scam! Real virus warnings never ask you to call a number or pay. Close the tab (or the whole browser), don't call, and tell a grown-up."],
  ["i won a prize online | free robux | free gift card offer", "Offers like free Robux, V-Bucks, phones or gift cards are almost always scams trying to steal your account or info. Don't click and don't enter any details."],
  ["how do i know if a link is safe | is this link safe | hover over a link", "Hover over the link to see where it really goes. Be careful with misspelled names (like micros0ft.com), strange endings or shortened links from strangers. If unsure, type the website address yourself."],
  ["what should i do if i clicked a bad link | i clicked a scam link | i think i got hacked", "Don't type anything into the page. Close it, tell a trusted adult, change the password for any account you entered, and run a virus scan. Turn on two-factor authentication if you can."],
  ["how do i stay safe online | internet safety tips | online safety", "Keep personal info private (full name, address, school, passwords), only chat with people you know in real life, don't download from sketchy sites, be kind, and tell a trusted adult if anything feels wrong."],
  ["what personal info should i keep private | what not to share online | private information", "Don't share your home address, phone number, school name, passwords, birthday, or photos that show where you live. Think before you post — things online can last forever."],
  ["how do i back up my files | backup my computer | save my files somewhere safe", "Keep a copy of important files in a second place: an external hard drive or USB stick, or cloud storage like OneDrive, Google Drive or iCloud. A good rule is 3 copies, on 2 kinds of storage, with 1 kept somewhere else."],
  ["why should i back up | what is a backup | do i need a backup", "A backup is a spare copy of your files. If your computer breaks, gets lost or gets a virus, you won't lose your photos, homework and projects."],
  ["what is the cloud | what is cloud storage | where is the cloud", "'The cloud' just means other companies' computers on the internet that store your files, so you can reach them from any device. OneDrive, Google Drive and iCloud are examples."],
  ["what is a screenshot | what does screenshot mean | why take a screenshot", "A screenshot is a picture of what's on your screen. It's handy for saving info or showing someone a problem."],
  ["how do i take a screenshot on windows | screenshot on a real pc | windows screenshot", "Press **Windows + Shift + S** and drag to capture part of the screen, or press **Print Screen** for the whole screen. Paste it with **Ctrl + V**."],
  ["how do i take a screenshot on a mac | mac screenshot | cmd shift 4", "Press **Cmd + Shift + 3** for the whole screen or **Cmd + Shift + 4** to drag a box. The picture saves to your desktop."],
  ["how do i take a screenshot on my phone | screenshot on iphone | screenshot on android", "On most iPhones press the **Side button + Volume Up** together. On most Android phones press **Power + Volume Down** together."],
  ["how do i type faster | improve typing speed | learn to touch type", "Learn touch typing: rest your fingers on the home row (**A S D F** and **J K L ;**), look at the screen instead of the keys, and practice a little every day with a free typing game. Accuracy first — speed comes later!"],
  ["what is the home row | where do my fingers go on the keyboard | f and j bumps", "The home row is **A S D F** for your left hand and **J K L ;** for your right. The little bumps on **F** and **J** help you find it without looking."],
  ["how do i search the internet better | google search tips | how to use a search engine well", "Use a few key words instead of a whole sentence, put \"quotes\" around exact phrases, add a minus to skip words (like jaguar -car), and use site: to search one website (like site:nasa.gov moon). Check a couple of trustworthy sources."],
  ["how do i know if a website is trustworthy | is this website reliable | fake news", "Check who made the site, whether it has a date and sources, and whether other trusted sites say the same thing. Be careful of sites that are mostly ads or try to make you angry or scared."],
  ["what is a search engine | what is google | what is bing", "A search engine is a website that finds pages on the internet for you. Google, Bing and DuckDuckGo are popular search engines."],
  ["what is a web browser | browser vs search engine | what is chrome", "A web browser is the app you use to visit websites, like Edge, Chrome, Safari or Firefox. A search engine (like Google or Bing) is a website you visit inside the browser to find other pages."],
  ["what is a url | what is a web address | what does https mean", "A URL is a website's address, like https://example.com. **https** means the connection is encrypted, which keeps what you send private — but it doesn't prove a site is honest."],
  ["what is ram | what is memory in a computer | ram vs storage", "**RAM** is the computer's short-term memory for things running right now — more RAM lets you run more at once. **Storage** (SSD or hard drive) is long-term space where files are kept even when it's off."],
  ["what is a cpu | what is a processor | what does the cpu do", "The **CPU** (processor) is the computer's brain. It follows instructions and does calculations for everything you do."],
  ["what is a gpu | what is a graphics card | why do games need a gpu", "A **GPU** (graphics card) draws pictures on the screen. It's super fast at graphics, which is why games and video editing love a good GPU."],
  ["what is an ssd | ssd vs hard drive | what is a hard drive", "An **SSD** stores files on fast chips with no moving parts. A hard drive (**HDD**) uses a spinning disk — it's cheaper for lots of space but slower."],
  ["what is an operating system | what is an os | windows vs mac", "An operating system (OS) is the main software that runs a computer and lets apps work. Windows, macOS, Linux, ChromeOS, iOS and Android are all operating systems."],
  ["what is a gigabyte | how big is a gb | kb mb gb tb", "Storage is measured in bytes: about 1,000 kilobytes (KB) make a megabyte (MB), 1,000 MB make a gigabyte (GB), and 1,000 GB make a terabyte (TB). A song is about 5 MB; a movie can be several GB."],
  ["what is bluetooth | how does bluetooth work | bluetooth meaning", "Bluetooth is a short-range wireless connection for things like headphones, mice, keyboards and speakers. Turn it on, put the device in pairing mode, then pick it from your Bluetooth list."],
  ["what is wifi | how does wifi work | wifi vs internet", "Wi-Fi is a wireless connection between your device and a router. The router is connected to the internet, so Wi-Fi is how your device reaches it without a cable."],
  ["what is a usb | usb port | usb c vs usb a", "USB is the common plug for connecting devices and charging. **USB-A** is the older flat rectangle; **USB-C** is the small oval one that fits either way up."],
  ["how do i connect to a printer | add a printer | printer not working", "Make sure the printer is on and connected to the same Wi-Fi (or plugged in by USB). On Windows, go to **Settings** → **Bluetooth & devices** → **Printers & scanners** → **Add device**. If it's stuck, turn the printer off and on."],
  ["how do i connect headphones | pair bluetooth headphones | headphones not working", "For wired headphones, plug them in fully. For Bluetooth, turn on pairing mode on the headphones, then on your device open Bluetooth settings and choose them from the list."],
  ["what is a virus | what is malware | how do computers get viruses", "Malware is harmful software, like viruses, that can steal info or break things. It often sneaks in through sketchy downloads, fake ads and email attachments. Keep antivirus on, update often and only download from trusted places."],
  ["how do i scan for viruses | antivirus | is my computer infected", "On Windows, open **Windows Security** → **Virus & threat protection** → **Quick scan**. Keep it turned on and updated."],
  ["is it safe to download this | how do i download safely | safe downloads", "Only download from official app stores or the real company's website. Avoid 'free' versions of paid games or apps, and ask a grown-up before installing anything."],
  ["how do i free up space | disk is full | storage almost full", "Delete files and apps you don't use, empty the Recycle Bin, clear old downloads, and move photos and videos to cloud storage or an external drive. On Windows, try **Settings** → **System** → **Storage** → **Cleanup recommendations**."],
  ["how do i uninstall a program on windows | remove an app from windows 11 | delete a real app", "Open **Settings** → **Apps** → **Installed apps**, click the **⋯** next to the app and choose **Uninstall**."],
  ["what is dark mode good for | is dark mode better for your eyes | why use dark mode", "Dark mode uses light text on a dark background. Many people find it more comfortable at night, and it can save battery on phones with OLED screens."],
  ["how long should i use the computer | screen time tips | eye strain", "Take breaks! Try the 20-20-20 rule: every 20 minutes, look at something 20 feet away for 20 seconds. Sit up straight, keep the screen at arm's length and stretch now and then."],
  ["what is an app | app vs program | what does app mean", "An app (short for application) is a program that does a job for you, like a game, a web browser or a calculator. On computers they're often called programs."],
  ["what is a pdf | why use pdf | how do i make a pdf", "A PDF is a document that looks the same on every device. To make one, choose **Print** and pick **Microsoft Print to PDF** (Windows) or **Save as PDF**, or use **Save As** → PDF in Word."],
  ["how do i right click on a laptop | right click on a trackpad | two finger click", "On most laptops, click the bottom-right corner of the touchpad or tap with two fingers. On a Mac, click with two fingers or hold **Control** while clicking."],
  ["what does double click mean | how to double click | double click not working", "Double-click means pressing the left mouse button twice quickly. It usually opens files and apps. If it's not working, try clicking a little faster."],
  ["how do i copy text on my phone | copy and paste on iphone | copy paste on android", "Press and hold on the text until it highlights, drag the handles to pick what you want, then tap **Copy**. To paste, press and hold where you want it and tap **Paste**."],
  ["how do i close apps on my phone | force close an app on iphone | phone app frozen", "On iPhone, swipe up from the bottom and pause, then swipe the app up and away. On Android, tap the recent apps button (or swipe up and hold) and swipe the app away."],
  ["how do i restart my phone | phone is frozen | reboot my phone", "Most phones restart by holding the power button (on newer iPhones, side button + a volume button) until a power menu appears, then choosing **Restart** or sliding to power off and turning it back on."],
  ["how do i update my phone | phone software update | update iphone", "On iPhone: **Settings** → **General** → **Software Update**. On Android: **Settings** → **System** (or **Software update**) → check for updates. Plug in and use Wi-Fi first."],
  ["my phone storage is full | free space on phone | phone says storage full", "Delete apps you don't use, clear old videos and photos (after backing them up), and clear big message threads. Check **Settings** → **Storage** to see what's using the most space."]
);
